{"name":"Redbox","hex":"#94332f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Redbox","blocks":[{"text":"Redbox was an American video rental and streaming media company, based in Oakbrook Terrace, Illinois, west of Chicago. Redbox specialized in automated DVD rental kiosks, and operated transactional and ad-supported streaming video and television services. From 2022 until its liquidation, Redbox was a wholly owned subsidiary of Chicken Soup for the Soul Entertainment."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Redbox"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Redbox_Kiosk_Closing_Notice.jpg/500px-Redbox_Kiosk_Closing_Notice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Redbox_Kiosk_Closing_Notice.jpg/1280px-Redbox_Kiosk_Closing_Notice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Redbox_Kiosk_Closing_Notice.jpg/500px-Redbox_Kiosk_Closing_Notice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Shutdown notice on a Redbox kiosk at an Albertsons store in Chula Vista, California","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARedbox_Kiosk_Closing_Notice.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Redbox_kiosk_in_front_of_a_Loaf_%27N_Jug_in_Gillette%2C_Wyoming.jpg/500px-Redbox_kiosk_in_front_of_a_Loaf_%27N_Jug_in_Gillette%2C_Wyoming.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Redbox_kiosk_in_front_of_a_Loaf_%27N_Jug_in_Gillette%2C_Wyoming.jpg/1280px-Redbox_kiosk_in_front_of_a_Loaf_%27N_Jug_in_Gillette%2C_Wyoming.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Redbox_kiosk_in_front_of_a_